      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KICKER MINI (1) got the job done again after leading them home to make it two on the bounce at this track over 300m (17.37). Is yet to taste defeat in two starts from this draw. Expected to go well again. PIPPA (2) is a capable type and proved too strong last time to win by one length at this track in a handy 17.42 beating Dolly Dawn. Smart beginner who should take advantage of the low draw. Makes plenty of appeal on the back of that last-start win. MISS TWIX (4) turned in a solid run last start over 300m at this track finishing 4th and beaten only 4 lengths (17.62). Form here at the trip sound including four wins. Safe beginner but has a tricky box to overcome. Key runner who gets her chance to atone.",
